    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "title": "Note: Usage",
      "pos": [
        30,
        1830
      ],
      "size": [
        460,
        540
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 11,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Qwen Image 2.1 - Edit / Reference Workflow\n\nEdits an existing image or generates a new one from a reference, using the same\nmodel as the text-to-image workflow (int8 copies on the comfyui-models volume).\n\n1. Pick or upload the image in **Input Image 1** — plus **Input Image 2 / 3** if\n   you want multiple references (drag & drop onto the canvas, or upload from your\n   machine with `modal volume put comfyui-input my_photo.png /` and select it in\n   the dropdown).\n2. Write the instruction in the encode node's *prompt*. Refer to the loaded image\n   as `<image1>`, e.g. \"make the sky in <image1> sunset colored, keep everything\n   else unchanged\" (edit), or \"generate a new fantasy castle in the same\n   architectural style as <image1>\" (reference-based generation).\n3. Queue Prompt. The output size follows the first input image (<image1>) by default.\n\n**Multiple references:** **Input Image 2** and **Input Image 3** are pre-wired\nas `<image2>` and `<image3>` — set their files, or delete those two links for\nsingle-image runs. E.g. \"put the shirt from <image2> on the person in\n<image1>\". Need more? Connect extra *Load Image* nodes to the empty image\nslots — the encode node accepts up to 16 references.\n\n**Size controls:** `resolution` (encode node) is the total pixel budget for the\nreferences, **shared** across them — raise it to 2048 when using several:\n1024 by default, 2048 for native 2K, 0 = keep original sizes. For a\nfixed custom output size instead, set the *Empty Latent Image* width/height and\nflip the *If/Else Switch* to **true**.\n\nSampler: 25 steps, cfg 1, euler + simple (official template defaults).\nAPI version for scripts: `workflows/qwen_image_2.1_edit_api.json` (POST to /prompt)."
      ]
    }
